WEBVTT

00:00:00.456 --> 00:00:03.604
Let's embrace...

00:00:03.604 --> 00:00:05.982
Being together like this...

00:00:05.982 --> 00:00:09.906
...is something I'll never forget!

00:00:09.906 --> 00:00:13.318
Forever...

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:15.834
...under this sky...

00:00:15.836 --> 00:00:18.447
...we'll walk together!

00:00:19.842 --> 00:00:21.136
In this beauty...

00:00:21.139 --> 00:00:22.248
...that I'm dreaming...

00:00:22.256 --> 00:00:23.293
...the world's just a...

00:00:23.307 --> 00:00:24.428
...merry, merry-go-round!

00:00:24.678 --> 00:00:26.015
With more dreaming...

00:00:26.026 --> 00:00:27.086
...and more loving...

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:28.170
...my heart is a...

00:00:28.184 --> 00:00:29.395
...merry, merry-go-round!

00:00:29.397 --> 00:00:30.690
Luvly, merry-go-round!

00:00:30.905 --> 00:00:33.081
Getting ready for a good morning...

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:35.769
...I say 'good morning', then I chat and run.

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:37.942
A lovely life every day...

00:00:37.952 --> 00:00:40.641
...is my wish for you, my sweet heart!

00:00:40.641 --> 00:00:42.749
A, B, C, D, E, F, G!

00:00:42.752 --> 00:00:45.397
A lack of vitamins isn't healthy.

00:00:45.413 --> 00:00:47.528
1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7!

00:00:47.541 --> 00:00:50.609
Bring along your favorite and let's go!

00:00:53.088 --> 00:00:56.466
Rolling rainbow star!

00:00:56.471 --> 00:00:58.839
If you go there...

00:00:58.847 --> 00:01:02.831
...you'll surely find it!

00:01:02.842 --> 00:01:06.211
Lovely roller coaster!

00:01:06.213 --> 00:01:08.690
Under this sky...

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:11.348
...its a total pleasure!

00:01:13.615 --> 00:01:16.060
Being together like this...

00:01:16.062 --> 00:01:19.592
...is something I'll never forget!

00:01:23.285 --> 00:01:25.786
Under this sky...

00:01:25.786 --> 00:01:28.278
...we'll walk together!

00:01:37.094 --> 00:01:37.720
Come in.

00:01:40.389 --> 00:01:43.643
Ah! It's been a long time, Dan-Sensei!

00:01:44.310 --> 00:01:45.353
Tooyama-kun!

00:01:46.103 --> 00:01:48.397
You didn't have to come all the way down here.

00:01:48.397 --> 00:01:50.399
I would have come to you, myself.

00:01:50.816 --> 00:01:51.901
Come on, why should you,

00:01:52.735 --> 00:01:56.405
a man who has worked his way up to the
position of Police Superintendent so quickly,

00:01:56.781 --> 00:01:59.825
cater to a mere private detective like me?

00:02:00.409 --> 00:02:02.536
What are you saying, Dan-Sensei?

00:02:03.996 --> 00:02:07.416
The Dan Morihiko I remember from when
I first joined the police force was a man

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:11.504
who not only shone as the ace of the
headquarters at the young age of 27,

00:02:11.587 --> 00:02:15.508
but was also called a potential
candidate for Commissioner!

00:02:16.634 --> 00:02:20.888
What's more, compared to what we saw of
you in the days that followed, I'm nothing!

00:02:21.514 --> 00:02:23.724
You're exaggerating, as usual.

00:02:24.642 --> 00:02:27.019
So, what brings you here today?

00:02:28.813 --> 00:02:30.731
Oh, no! Did my idiotic son...?

00:02:35.736 --> 00:02:38.030
No, no, it's not about Kinta-kun...

00:02:40.282 --> 00:02:40.908
Annam!

00:02:51.627 --> 00:02:53.212
Ugh... This is a...!

00:02:54.255 --> 00:02:55.256
It's a listening bug.

00:02:55.965 --> 00:02:58.009
Inside the Police Headquarters...

00:02:58.884 --> 00:03:01.762
I didn't even notice it! Who in the world...?

00:03:02.722 --> 00:03:03.931
Pluto.

00:03:06.225 --> 00:03:08.519
It's Pluto, Tooyama-kun.

00:03:09.311 --> 00:03:12.064
Oh! But, Pluto was...

00:03:12.356 --> 00:03:14.650
It's the organization that I, Dan
Morihiko, at the risk of my life,

00:03:14.650 --> 00:03:17.653
and by paying a huge price,
once managed to destroy...

00:03:18.654 --> 00:03:21.323
You mean to tell me they've
resumed their activities?

00:03:23.034 --> 00:03:27.580
As a matter of fact, Tooyama-kun, I've come to
talk to you about none other than that matter.

00:03:28.497 --> 00:03:34.837
In a case several pupils took on in Karuizawa,
we detected signs of Pluto's involvement.

00:03:35.504 --> 00:03:36.589
I don't believe it!

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:39.592
I'm warning you, Tooyama-kun.

00:03:39.967 --> 00:03:42.928
They are capable of using their precision plastic
surgery and masquerading technology...

00:03:42.928 --> 00:03:46.932
...to disguise themselves as anyone
and infiltrate any system.

00:03:47.475 --> 00:03:49.101
The police are no exception.

00:03:50.102 --> 00:03:52.438
There's only one way to identify them by sight.

00:03:53.355 --> 00:03:56.525
A member will have a mark
somewhere on their body:

00:03:58.402 --> 00:04:00.738
The Pluto Crest.

00:04:01.697 --> 00:04:03.949
To actually mark a bug...

00:04:04.408 --> 00:04:05.785
How bold of them!

00:04:07.828 --> 00:04:10.664
We must figure out how to prevent their
activities before they happen,

00:04:10.956 --> 00:04:13.542
and exterminate them before it's too late.

00:04:15.377 --> 00:04:21.383
I, Dan Morihiko, will stake my reputation as a detective on this battle with Pluto.

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:31.727
This one is... from DDS' Class Q.

00:04:34.230 --> 00:04:35.981
But, why this one?

00:04:37.024 --> 00:04:40.361
You do not need to know that, Miss Kaori.

00:04:40.903 --> 00:04:45.324
Oh. Certainly, sir. I will be on it at once.

00:04:49.453 --> 00:04:54.166
Targeted Megu

00:04:57.545 --> 00:05:01.048
Kyuu said he only wanted to expose
the trick behind the sealed room,

00:05:01.674 --> 00:05:04.093
but I'm sure he was worried about the rumor.

00:05:04.593 --> 00:05:08.514
All boys are weak towards older,
beautiful women, aren't they?

00:05:14.895 --> 00:05:15.646
Yeah?

00:05:16.564 --> 00:05:19.066
To get a nice body....

00:05:19.733 --> 00:05:20.985
Oh! Never mind!

00:05:21.569 --> 00:05:22.194
Huh?

00:05:23.445 --> 00:05:25.447
How unusual: thoughts about sex appeal.

00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:35.207
You sure talk about Kyuu-kun a lot.

00:05:38.377 --> 00:05:40.045
W-What do you mean?

00:05:40.546 --> 00:05:43.757
I always talk about everyone from Class Q...

00:05:46.385 --> 00:05:50.389
You talk about Kyuu-kun
and Ryu-kun all the time,

00:05:50.598 --> 00:05:53.684
and only a little bit about the other two.

00:05:54.226 --> 00:05:55.811
Um... well...

00:05:56.437 --> 00:05:58.105
I want to meet them...

00:05:59.481 --> 00:06:03.861
I have an idea, Megu! Why don't you bring
your two princes over tomorrow?

00:06:05.529 --> 00:06:06.572
It's decided, then!

00:06:07.281 --> 00:06:08.741
What should I cook?

00:06:08.908 --> 00:06:11.076
Wait, Sis!

00:06:11.827 --> 00:06:14.288
You can bring the other two, if you wish.

00:06:20.294 --> 00:06:21.712
So here's a problem.

00:06:22.588 --> 00:06:30.095
Which detective stated that two plus
two is always equal to four?

00:06:30.799 --> 00:06:31.886
Tooyama-kun!

00:06:33.515 --> 00:06:34.725
How I would I know that?!

00:06:35.226 --> 00:06:36.310
Einstein?

00:06:36.936 --> 00:06:37.895
Wrong!

00:06:38.520 --> 00:06:39.271
How about Megu?

00:06:41.565 --> 00:06:42.816
I don't know.

00:06:43.859 --> 00:06:44.526
Kyuu?

00:06:45.569 --> 00:06:49.865
Well, two plus two should naturally be four.

00:06:49.865 --> 00:06:52.660
To bother stating something as obvious as that...

00:06:52.952 --> 00:06:53.744
Um...

00:06:54.954 --> 00:06:56.997
That French inspector who cracked alibis!

00:06:57.289 --> 00:06:58.374
Wrong!

00:06:58.749 --> 00:07:01.085
Then, paradoxically speaking,
it was Father Brown!

00:07:01.210 --> 00:07:02.253
Wrong!

00:07:03.712 --> 00:07:05.256
Just tell us!

00:07:06.257 --> 00:07:11.387
The famous "Thinking Machine," Professor
Augustus S. F. X. Van Dusen!

00:07:11.887 --> 00:07:12.763
Huh?

00:07:13.430 --> 00:07:15.557
Ah! Of course!

00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:17.643
As if you knew!

00:07:23.023 --> 00:07:27.027
Getting two consecutive days
of self-study is great.

00:07:27.111 --> 00:07:30.030
Really? I thought you hated classes.

00:07:30.447 --> 00:07:31.782
They're nice once in a while!

00:07:31.824 --> 00:07:33.993
Really, Kinta, don't you always like it that way?

00:07:33.590 --> 00:07:34.952
H-Hey, Kyuu!

00:07:36.787 --> 00:07:37.538
Um...

00:07:39.915 --> 00:07:41.875
Why don't you come over to my place today?

00:07:42.584 --> 00:07:45.129
My sister asked me to bring you over.

00:07:45.713 --> 00:07:46.338
Um...

00:07:51.593 --> 00:07:53.304
You guys are invited, as well.

00:07:53.929 --> 00:07:56.807
My sister excited and she's making
a home-cooked meal.

00:07:57.391 --> 00:08:00.352
Hey, you didn't have to go to all that trouble.

00:08:01.020 --> 00:08:03.981
You could've just ordered pizza or katsudon.

00:08:04.565 --> 00:08:06.859
Sorry, I'm going to go home and get some sleep.

00:08:07.526 --> 00:08:10.654
I've been so busy debugging my game
software, that my lack of sleep is just...

00:08:12.239 --> 00:08:16.702
How dare ya refuse Megu's invitation like that! You're coming!

00:08:19.038 --> 00:08:20.289
Oh! Ryu-kun!

00:08:22.458 --> 00:08:24.501
My sister told me to ask you, as well.

00:08:25.544 --> 00:08:28.088
I can't. I've got plans.

00:08:28.589 --> 00:08:30.507
Oh... is that so?

00:08:33.010 --> 00:08:36.847
But, thanks for the invitation.

00:08:40.351 --> 00:08:45.356
<i>This feeling I yet... It's the same as I felt when
I first met Ryu-kun on Kirisaki Island.</i>

00:08:47.149 --> 00:08:48.859
<i>As if I'd met him somewhere before.</i>

00:08:49.526 --> 00:08:51.695
<i>But that can't be.</i>

00:08:51.695 --> 00:08:54.990
<i>I couldn't forget him; I have
a photographic memory.</i>

00:08:58.410 --> 00:08:59.620
Well, I'm leaving.

00:09:04.166 --> 00:09:07.086
Geez. Ryu ls as unsociable as ever, eh?

00:09:07.419 --> 00:09:09.546
I wanted to go home, too!

00:09:09.880 --> 00:09:13.050
Oh, dear His share will be leftover.

00:09:13.300 --> 00:09:14.218
You want to invite someone else?

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:25.312
Yo, Class Q! Long time no see!

00:09:29.733 --> 00:09:32.820
Ryu-sama, do you like it there at DDS?

00:09:33.404 --> 00:09:36.532
Yeah, I've learned a lot from them.

00:09:37.449 --> 00:09:38.242
Learned?

00:09:39.701 --> 00:09:41.203
That's nice to hear.

00:09:42.204 --> 00:09:47.459
Ever since you joined DDS,
you've become full of life.

00:09:48.127 --> 00:09:49.962
And we are happy about that.

00:09:51.880 --> 00:09:56.343
Just... don't forget your position.

00:09:57.219 --> 00:09:58.095
I understand that.

00:09:59.012 --> 00:10:04.560
One more thing. Please don't get too
intimate with the other students.

00:10:05.644 --> 00:10:10.691
We don't want you to go astray
by mixing with such people.

00:10:11.066 --> 00:10:13.402
Have you been spying on me, Yurie-san?

00:10:14.194 --> 00:10:15.612
Nothing like that.

00:10:16.405 --> 00:10:20.534
Since your grandfather has given me the
responsibility of looking after you,

00:10:20.909 --> 00:10:23.162
I'm just naturally concerned.

00:10:26.582 --> 00:10:33.714
Really? So, Megumi-chan's sister is a
19-year-old softmore in college?

00:10:34.840 --> 00:10:37.134
Now, it didn't have to be him!

00:10:37.384 --> 00:10:40.804
Yeah, I agree. Well, he's just a spare.

00:10:41.180 --> 00:10:43.015
You guys say something?

00:10:43.140 --> 00:10:44.475
Ah... no, nothing.

00:10:45.225 --> 00:10:46.768
<i>A spare, huh?</i>

00:10:48.479 --> 00:10:49.146
Hey, Megu.

00:10:50.230 --> 00:10:52.065
So, what's your sister like?

00:10:52.441 --> 00:10:56.653
Um... it's kind of weird for me to
describe her, since we're sisters.

00:10:57.029 --> 00:10:58.155
But I'd say she's very pretty.

00:10:59.031 --> 00:10:59.698
Pretty!

00:11:02.576 --> 00:11:03.660
Hottie!

00:11:04.828 --> 00:11:06.872
College girl!

00:11:07.331 --> 00:11:09.791
Hey, wait! What's with all that fantasizing?!

00:11:13.795 --> 00:11:17.758
So what type of guys does your sister like?

00:11:20.093 --> 00:11:22.513
Well she's rather methodical and cleanly,

00:11:22.513 --> 00:11:24.765
so I'd guess she doesn't like men who
are disorganized and unclean.

00:11:24.890 --> 00:11:25.682
Damn it!

00:11:32.022 --> 00:11:34.525
Too late to change yourself now.

00:11:34.983 --> 00:11:41.156
I'm the one for her, a student at Tokyo
University, and With an of 180.

00:11:42.407 --> 00:11:45.369
Despite attending the National Institute
of Brainpower Development with Megu,

00:11:45.369 --> 00:11:48.372
she's never invited you over.

00:11:49.122 --> 00:11:52.209
Get lost, you high schooler! I'm older than ya!

00:11:52.334 --> 00:11:54.169
Who cares about age?!

00:11:54.586 --> 00:11:56.338
This has turned into an ugly quarrel, hasn't it?

00:11:56.922 --> 00:11:57.548
Yeah.

00:12:03.303 --> 00:12:05.389
Wow, you sure live in a nice place!

00:12:05.639 --> 00:12:06.598
You think so?

00:12:07.015 --> 00:12:09.977
The view is just perfect!
Is it huge inside, as well?

00:12:10.477 --> 00:12:14.565
Not really, but my parents have
been abroad for a while now,

00:12:14.565 --> 00:12:17.651
so with just myself and my sister
here, it's plenty big enough.

00:12:21.613 --> 00:12:22.281
Huh?

00:12:24.741 --> 00:12:25.909
What's wrong, Megu?

00:12:26.326 --> 00:12:28.662
The key won't turn.

00:12:29.079 --> 00:12:29.746
Key?

00:12:36.420 --> 00:12:39.590
Oh, no! The key doesn't work!

00:12:39.840 --> 00:12:42.718
Maybe the key's become deformed with time.

00:12:43.260 --> 00:12:44.928
Or maybe you've got a burglar.

00:12:49.099 --> 00:12:51.101
It's just a joke, guys!

00:12:52.060 --> 00:12:54.855
He may be right about the burglar, you know.

00:12:56.773 --> 00:12:59.401
In burgling cases, if the lock is forcibly opened,

00:12:59.860 --> 00:13:04.364
the keyhole often gets deformed and
the key doesn't work anymore.

00:13:05.949 --> 00:13:08.535
Then, you mean to say, in Megu's apartment...

00:13:10.537 --> 00:13:12.039
There's a burglar!

00:13:26.069 --> 00:13:29.822
Oh! What do I do?! A Burglar?!

00:13:31.074 --> 00:13:32.116
Calm down!

00:13:33.660 --> 00:13:35.453
Can it, both of ya!”

00:13:35.954 --> 00:13:37.538
Leave it to me!

00:13:38.248 --> 00:13:41.960
Hey, shouldn't you use the
picking tool for picking?

00:13:42.335 --> 00:13:45.546
But, we haven't really learned how
to use it properly yet, have we?

00:13:45.588 --> 00:13:47.715
Oh, that's right.

00:13:54.264 --> 00:13:58.351
That bastard!!!

00:14:02.230 --> 00:14:04.065
Whew! Finally open!

00:14:07.068 --> 00:14:09.487
My Lock!

00:14:11.781 --> 00:14:13.366
That was amazing.

00:14:26.212 --> 00:14:28.381
Hey, there's no one here.

00:14:28.798 --> 00:14:31.884
Then, the lock was only broken? Sorry...

00:14:32.176 --> 00:14:35.972
Sorry?! You broke my lock!

00:14:46.107 --> 00:14:49.360
I guess we jumped to conclusions
too early. So, just relax now.

00:14:49.610 --> 00:14:51.279
This is my house Kinta!

00:14:51.321 --> 00:14:52.613
Yeah, yeah!

00:14:52.905 --> 00:14:53.656
We weren't wrong.

00:14:56.451 --> 00:14:57.285
We weren't wrong.

00:14:59.162 --> 00:15:01.456
This house was broken into by a burglar.

00:15:08.004 --> 00:15:09.005
Damn!

00:15:10.590 --> 00:15:11.716
But, how do you know?

00:15:12.258 --> 00:15:15.678
Hey, Megu can you use your
photographic memory?

00:15:15.678 --> 00:15:19.390
Is there anything different about this room?

00:15:20.141 --> 00:15:21.434
O-Okay.

00:15:22.852 --> 00:15:23.686
Um...

00:15:43.498 --> 00:15:45.625
-here are more dishes in the cupboard!

00:15:46.793 --> 00:15:48.795
Huh? How can that be?

00:15:48.795 --> 00:15:52.090
Usually in burglaries, the number of items decreases doesn't it?

00:15:52.256 --> 00:15:53.591
So, then...

00:15:54.008 --> 00:15:55.385
You can't mean...?

00:15:58.012 --> 00:16:01.974
So, if the burglar was inside when we arrived,

00:16:02.725 --> 00:16:05.269
He couldn't have escaped from the window,
because it's on the twelfth floor.

00:16:05.895 --> 00:16:08.356
Given that, he had to hide himself somewhere.

00:16:08.898 --> 00:16:11.609
He just had to move the stuff that
was in his way somewhere else.

00:16:12.777 --> 00:16:17.615
I get it Megumi-chan, where did
you keep the other dishes?

00:16:18.116 --> 00:16:21.911
There. Behind that wooden door.

00:16:22.036 --> 00:16:25.665
Aha, the perfect size for accommodating a single human being.

00:16:26.874 --> 00:16:27.959
That means...

00:16:28.543 --> 00:16:31.546
The burglar's inside it?

00:16:32.338 --> 00:16:35.508
All right. Megumi-chan, get
me some kind of a rope.

00:16:35.967 --> 00:16:36.884
O-Okay.

00:16:39.137 --> 00:16:43.307
Great. Now, I'll tie this laundry
rope around the cupboard.

00:16:43.891 --> 00:16:45.476
And you, kid, help me.

00:16:45.852 --> 00:16:46.727
Me?!

00:16:46.936 --> 00:16:48.396
You've got me for that stuff.

00:16:52.817 --> 00:16:54.735
Here, tie this around.

00:16:54.861 --> 00:16:57.155
What? But it's stuck.

00:16:57.155 --> 00:16:58.239
They fell for it, didn't they?
What? But it's stuck.

00:16:58.239 --> 00:16:58.948
They fell for it, didn't they?

00:16:58.948 --> 00:17:02.743
They think I'm hiding in that cupboard.

00:17:03.202 --> 00:17:05.371
After all, they're nothing but a bunch
of kids playing detective.

00:17:06.247 --> 00:17:09.292
They can't beat a pro.

00:17:30.104 --> 00:17:30.688
Kinta!

00:17:31.022 --> 00:17:31.898
Piece of cake!

00:17:34.066 --> 00:17:35.735
It was nothing for me.

00:17:37.028 --> 00:17:38.696
H-How?

00:17:38.696 --> 00:17:40.907
I thought he was inside the cupboard.

00:17:41.115 --> 00:17:43.993
That was just a distraction. You didn't get it?

00:17:44.285 --> 00:17:45.536
What was that?!

00:17:45.953 --> 00:17:48.247
An odd burglar, wasn't he?

00:17:50.124 --> 00:17:51.709
Well, I'll leave the rest to you.

00:17:52.627 --> 00:17:54.795
Thanks for your cooperation. See you later.

00:17:58.257 --> 00:18:03.429
This is Nanami. It seems the intruder in Minami
Megumi's house was just an ordinary thief.

00:18:03.888 --> 00:18:05.890
Is that so? Come back here.

00:18:06.265 --> 00:18:06.891
Yes, sir.

00:18:14.732 --> 00:18:17.902
The shoes and other dishes were
stuffed inside the closet.

00:18:18.402 --> 00:18:21.072
We'd better put things back where they
belong before my sister gets home.

00:18:22.073 --> 00:18:28.454
Hah! What a stupid burglar... to break into
the house of a student of DDS' Class Q!

00:18:29.080 --> 00:18:33.501
But, how did you figure out that the cupboard
was only a distraction, Kyuu?

00:18:34.126 --> 00:18:38.798
Huh? Ah... Well, if he had
intended to use the cupboard,

00:18:39.090 --> 00:18:41.801
he could've just stuffed everything
inside the closet.

00:18:43.010 --> 00:18:47.807
Instead, he chose to put them into a cupboard
with glass windows, to make them stand out.

00:18:48.849 --> 00:18:53.354
First and foremost ,though, he couldn't
have managed to escape from there.

00:18:54.272 --> 00:18:57.942
So I asked myself, "Why?" Then,
I tried to think like the burglar.

00:18:59.360 --> 00:19:03.072
When the culprit realized we had returned,
he tried to escape but couldn't,

00:19:03.072 --> 00:19:05.992
since this room is on the twelfth floor.

00:19:07.326 --> 00:19:10.705
So, for the time being, he decided
it was best to hide somewhere.

00:19:12.707 --> 00:19:17.878
Then, he would wait until we were
distracted, and quietly sneak away.

00:19:19.380 --> 00:19:21.591
Oh, right! If he was looking
for a chance to escape,

00:19:21.591 --> 00:19:24.594
the best place to hide would be the
shoe cupboard at the entrance-way.

00:19:24.844 --> 00:19:30.016
And there, Kyuu gave me two hints: The
entrance-way and your sister's character.

00:19:30.766 --> 00:19:33.477
The entrance-way and my sister's character?

00:19:34.228 --> 00:19:35.521
First the entrance-way.

00:19:35.521 --> 00:19:37.648
You guys must have noticed when we came in...

00:19:37.648 --> 00:19:39.817
...that her high heels were in bad shape.

00:19:42.320 --> 00:19:45.698
But, then again, Megu's sister
is not only a pretty girl...

00:19:46.699 --> 00:19:51.746
...with a nice body, who wears
mini-skirts... She's methodical.

00:19:52.288 --> 00:19:57.710
I said she was pretty and methodical, but never
mentioned a nice body or mini-skirts.

00:19:58.336 --> 00:20:04.091
Anyway, a methodical girl like her would
never leave her high heels like that.

00:20:04.508 --> 00:20:06.052
That's true, but...

00:20:06.719 --> 00:20:07.511
Can I take over?

00:20:10.556 --> 00:20:16.062
The culprit stuffed the shoes and the
shelf boards inside the closet.

00:20:16.896 --> 00:20:19.982
Then he entered and closed the doors.

00:20:21.233 --> 00:20:23.402
The high heels that were lying there...

00:20:23.569 --> 00:20:24.904
...got hit by the door.

00:20:25.571 --> 00:20:30.868
T-These shoes were in the exact same
position when we came in!

00:20:32.411 --> 00:20:37.458
Hiding in there, he would never have realized
that something like this had happened.

00:20:38.042 --> 00:20:38.668
Kyuu.

00:20:40.044 --> 00:20:44.590
So, when you first came in, you
had already noticed this?

00:20:44.757 --> 00:20:45.299
Right.

00:20:46.550 --> 00:20:47.218
. But...

00:20:47.718 --> 00:20:48.302
But?

00:20:49.428 --> 00:20:51.764
What in the world?! What happened to our lock?

00:20:56.060 --> 00:20:57.061
Would someone mind explaining?

00:20:57.436 --> 00:20:59.480
Well... this is... umm...

00:21:00.481 --> 00:21:02.358
Hello, elder Sister, it is my pleasure to meet you.

00:21:02.358 --> 00:21:03.442
<i>1
9</i>

00:21:03.442 --> 00:21:08.114
I'm Saburoumaru Yutaka, a Tokyo University
student with an IQ of 180.

00:21:08.739 --> 00:21:11.075
I'm Tooyama Kintaro.

00:21:13.202 --> 00:21:16.080
My favorite high heels!

00:21:18.916 --> 00:21:21.335
The table cloth I just bought yesterday!

00:21:21.961 --> 00:21:27.466
The tea set! And the shoes in the closet?!

00:21:28.634 --> 00:21:30.970
Next, do these dishes, please.

00:21:31.512 --> 00:21:35.099
I don't have to tell you where
they go, right, Megu?

00:21:35.641 --> 00:21:38.102
After all, you've got your
photographic memory to aid you.

00:21:42.106 --> 00:21:44.942
Whew! We just managed to
escape from an awful situation.

00:21:45.443 --> 00:21:47.653
It's a good thing we're on the shopping team.

00:21:48.195 --> 00:21:52.241
Megu and Kazuma are. probably being ordered around by her sister now.

00:21:55.536 --> 00:21:58.080
What's that intense face supposed to mean?

00:21:58.956 --> 00:21:59.582
Oh, nothing.

00:22:03.210 --> 00:22:03.961
Hey, Kinta.

00:22:05.129 --> 00:22:08.591
Why do you think the burglar put the
dishes inside the glass cupboard?

00:22:08.966 --> 00:22:13.262
Like you said, to get our attention...

00:22:13.387 --> 00:22:14.972
But that...

00:22:16.974 --> 00:22:22.104
That's as if he knew Megu would remember
the room's setup perfectly.

00:22:22.271 --> 00:22:26.066
In other words, that she had
a photographic memory.

00:22:29.570 --> 00:22:34.325
But hey that guy we caught looked like
no mare than an ordinary thief...

00:22:35.075 --> 00:22:37.453
...not a culprit from some secret criminal
organization, like the other day.

00:22:39.121 --> 00:22:40.206
I guess you're right.

00:22:41.332 --> 00:22:42.833
Maybe I'm just thinking too much.

00:22:45.836 --> 00:22:47.338
Hey, you alright?

00:22:48.172 --> 00:22:49.799
Come on! Hey!

00:22:56.972 --> 00:22:58.933
So that means, he was actually...

00:23:11.195 --> 00:23:15.616
My apologies, sir. It was
a close call with Class Q.

00:23:16.700 --> 00:23:20.454
And as for Minami Megumi, like you said,

00:23:20.955 --> 00:23:24.124
during the same period, the National Institute
of Brainpower Development...

00:23:29.296 --> 00:23:30.381
<i>Minami Megumi.</i>

00:23:31.173 --> 00:23:35.302
<i>We'll have to deal with her if circumstances
require us to do so.</i>

00:23:36.470 --> 00:23:37.555
<i>For Ryu-sama ’s sake.</i>

00:23:45.590 --> 00:23:47.425
THOSE THINGS REFLECTED IN YOUR EYES...

00:23:47.425 --> 00:23:49.761
...ARE DESTINED TO FALL APART.

00:23:49.761 --> 00:23:52.430
NO! NO! NO! NO! BELIEVING IN THAT...

00:23:52.430 --> 00:23:54.099
...IS UP TO YOU.

00:23:54.099 --> 00:23:56.101
LOVE AND KINDNESS...

00:23:56.101 --> 00:23:58.395
...OFTEN STEM FROM SELFISHNESS.

00:23:58.395 --> 00:24:00.939
IF YOU STILL PURSUE THEM...

00:24:00.939 --> 00:24:02.732
...YOU'RE JUST WANDERING AIMLESSLY.

00:24:03.441 --> 00:24:06.987
IT CAN SEEM BOTH FAR AND NEAR...

00:24:06.987 --> 00:24:10.615
THAT PLACE WHERE LOVE LIVES.

00:24:11.658 --> 00:24:13.702
THE UNSEEN STORY...

00:24:13.702 --> 00:24:16.121
...IS A MESSAGE TO YOU.

00:24:16.121 --> 00:24:18.248
YOU'RE USED TO WAITING FOR IT...

00:24:18.248 --> 00:24:19.791
...WITHOUT GIVING UP!

00:24:20.250 --> 00:24:22.460
THE UNSEEN STORY...

00:24:22.460 --> 00:24:24.671
EVEN WHEN WE'RE LOST...

00:24:25.171 --> 00:24:26.881
...CAN'T WE BELIEVE...

00:24:26.881 --> 00:24:30.385
...THAT WE CAN STILL DO IT?

00:24:31.177 --> 00:24:33.346
THE UNSEEN STORY...

00:24:33.346 --> 00:24:35.265
EVEN WHEN WERE LOST...

00:24:35.265 --> 00:24:37.642
...CAN'T WE BELIEVE...

00:24:37.684 --> 00:24:40.478
...THAT WE CAN STILL DO?

00:24:47.755 --> 00:24:49.089
An afternoon at the old building.

00:24:49.965 --> 00:24:51.717
The mystery lurking within.

00:24:52.509 --> 00:24:53.886
The secret behind the door that won't open.

00:24:54.887 --> 00:24:57.681
Where does the strange dragon door lead?

00:24:58.474 --> 00:25:03.103
And the identity of the shadow
which has been following us.

00:25:03.896 --> 00:25:05.147
There's only one answer!

00:25:07.316 --> 00:25:09.026
From your sister? For me?

00:25:09.234 --> 00:25:10.110
Yeah,open it

00:25:11.362 --> 00:25:13.155
Hey, this is a bill...

00:25:13.530 --> 00:25:15.532
Yeah, the cost of the lock you broke.

00:25:16.241 --> 00:25:17.242
Take care of it, okay?

00:25:20.079 --> 00:25:20.996
Not cute.

00:25:21.080 --> 00:25:21.956
What was that?!
